        "duration": 36.709999084472656,
        "text": "AI companies suspected behind bulk book orders. Booksellers suspect AI companies are secretly ordering massive quantities of books. For nearly a year, booksellers have noticed a trend of anonymous bulk orders with little regard for pricing. A recent investigation involved tracking an offer of 1,000 books, which ultimately led to an Amazon facility where workers reportedly altered the books for scanning efficiency. This raises concerns that AI companies are meticulously cataloging every published title for training purposes. Amazon has not commented on the situation, leaving many questions about the implications for the publishing industry.",
